ure off  during the holidays mike armstrong  global news  montreal millions of canadians have  relied on financial support from the  federal government to get through the  pandemic  now more than 410 000 people are being  asked to confirm  they were eligible for it the canada  revenue agency has sent them letters  asking them about their claims for the  canada emergency response benefit or  serb  the cra calls the letter educational it  explains what qualifies as earned income  to be eligible for the serb  and what does not the cra says not  everyone who receives a letter will be  required to pay the money back  8.9 million canadians have applied for  the benefit more than 81 billion dollars  has been paid out  those who don't meet the criteria are  being asked to repay the money by the  end of the year  to help get ahead of any problems at tax  time next year  a search is underway off the coast of  nova scotia for six missing scallop  fishers  search helicopters and vessels were  dispatched to an area near digby  after the fishing boat issued an  emergency alert shortly before 6  a.m hours later debris was spotted in  the water  and empty life rafts washed up on shore  there's been no sign of the boat itself  the maritime joint rescue coordination  center says waves were two meters high  at the time with winds topping  55 kilometers an hour and off the coast  of california a search is underway for a  sailor who is missing from a canadian  navy ship  canadian master sailor dwayne earl is  believed to have accidentally fallen  overboard hmcs winnipeg  early on monday the u.s coast guard is  helping with the search nearly a  thousand kilometers off the coast of san  francisco  the navy says earl was last seen at 8  a.m and discovered missing at 11 30 a.m  at which point the ship turned back to  look for him  a canadian famous for his clothing  company now in custody coming up the  allegations of sex crimes  involving peter nygard  a canadian who built an international  fashion brand named after himself is in  custody tonight  peter nygard was arrested in his  hometown of winnipeg following a u.s  extradition  request he's been indicted in the  southern district of new york on  multiple charges of sex trafficking  minors and racketeering  two of his own sons have filed lawsuits  against nygard  global's joe scarpelli was in the  courtroom where nygard appeared  joe donna peter nygaard  entered the courtroom in shackles a gray  hoodie and a white  face mask the fashion designer then  slowly made his way over to the  prisoner's box  glanced over at the media quickly before  turning his body towards the front of  the room and resting his head in his  hand  he looked nothing like the man you might  recognize in these pictures  nygaard was arrested monday night in  winnipeg following a request from the  u.s  justice department to begin extradition  proceedings to face  charges in the united states as part of  an ongoing investigation by the fbi  and new york police department the  79-year-old is facing a total of nine  charges the charges include conspiracy  to commit sex  trafficking sex trafficking of a minor  by force  fraud and several more dozens of women  joined a class  action lawsuit accusing nygard of rape  sexual assault and human  trafficking 12 of the victims were  minors when they say the crimes happened  lisa hamba is a florida attorney  representing the women  we've waited so long for this day to  come so long for peter nygar to be  criminally held accountable for his  crimes  and that day is finally here on the one  hand while they're so incredibly  overjoyed that he's being held  accountable  on the other hand it obviously brings up  all the pain and anguish  they've had to live with we spoke to  nygard's lawyer jay prober who says his  client denies  all allegations nygard's next court  appearance is scheduled for january 13th  but his lawyer says he'll be applying  for bail before then  donna joe scarpelli in winnip