arency and accountability  and that the party responsible for the  situation is investigating  itself largely in secret the report  also says there are indications of  incompetence recklessness and want and  disregard for innocent human life  the flight was shot down by iran's  revolutionary guard shortly after  takeoff from tehran on january 8th  all 176 people on board were killed  including 55 canadians  and 30 permanent residents  calls for change next cleveland's  baseball team finally makes a change  to its name  there is really no excuse anymore for  sports teams to keep using names and  logos that are offensive  times have changed and names that seemed  appropriate years ago  are now considered racist today  cleveland's major league baseball team  got with the program as eric sorenson  reports  the indians the name has been around  more than a hundred years in cleveland  parting with it won't be easy we're  never trying to be disrespectful  no but the team has been under mounting  pressure to recognize it is  disrespectful  it comes two years after the indians  dropped the offensive chief wahoo mascot  in a statement team owner paul dolan  acknowledges the name has detrimental  effects on native american people  the club adding we can unify our  community and bring people together  with a new name philip yenyo confronted  cleveland fans for years  it feels really good that that steps are  being taken  that our voices are being heard it's  taken decades for many u.s colleges to  abandon  indian-based nicknames and offensive  mascots in canada  mcgill university only dropped the term  redmond from men's varsity teams a year  ago they're now the redbirds  but pro sports teams have been  especially slow with enormous  investments in their iconic symbols  this past summer however protests  against systemic racism brought new  demands to drop such imagery once and  for all  the washington redskins finally gave in  after sponsors threatened to walk out  they're managing this season without a  nickname the edmonton eskimos are also  looking for a new team name  and now so is cleveland's baseball team  except  not for another year to give them time  to switch to a new name  and perhaps move some merchandise while  they can some say it's a mistake to  delay  once you say you're not going to use it  anymore you can't use it anymore  or else you're sort of defeating the  purpose of changing it still the name  will go  and that's the important thing says one  baseball writer it's not a popular  decision  in cleveland but it had to be it had to  be made several other sports teams still  have controversial names and the  question is  who might be next to change eric  sorenson global news  toronto and that is global national for  this tuesday i'm donna friesen  tonight's your canada is this picture  postcard shot of emerald lake lodge in  field  bc look at that there are beautiful  spots all over canada please email us  yours to viewers at globalnational.com  thanks for watching hope to see you here  again tomorrow take care of yourselves  bye-bye  [Applause]  [Music]
 

